  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
    Player: 'A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
    objective: 'Finish with each row in same-suit order from 2 through King, leaving the four gaps immediately to the right of the Kings.',
    gameplay: 'A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only legal successor cards can enter a gap: same suit and exactly one rank higher than the card on the left.',
      'A left-edge gap accepts only a 2.',
      'A gap to the right of a King is dead for that pass.',
      'After all redeals are used, if any row is incomplete, the game is lost.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'One player. Gaps is a patience (solitaire) game; a single player plays alone and makes all decisions about which cards to move into gaps and when to redeal.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'One shuffled deck and table space for four rows of thirteen cards.',
      dealing: 'Deal all 52 cards face up into four rows of thirteen. Remove all four aces, leaving four empty spaces.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Gaps is solitaire and has no ante or betting phase.',
      deal: 'Initial deal occurs once; redeal allowed only when no legal gap fill exists and redeals remain.',
      reveal_market: 'No market exists in Gaps; all cards are in tableau and stock handling only.',
      buy_market: 'Gaps has no purchasing mechanic or market row.',
      buy_stock: 'Stock cards are redealt by rule, not bought.',
      fold: 'Single-player patience has no fold action.',
      check: 'Gaps has no betting rounds and therefore no check action.',
      call: 'Gaps has no betting rounds and therefore no call action.',
      bet: 'No wagering mechanics are part of standard Gaps rules.',
      raise: 'No wagering mechanics are part of standard Gaps rules.',
      declare: 'There is no declaration phase in this patience game.',
      reveal_hand: 'All cards are face up on tableau, so hand reveal does not apply.',
      award_pot: 'Gaps has a binary win or loss outcome and no pot.',
      play_card: 'Left-edge gap only accepts a 2; gaps right of Kings are dead for the current pass.',
      draw: 'No draw-to-hand action exists; all cards remain in tableau flow.',
      discard: 'Only aces are discarded and only during setup.',
      pass: 'Turns are not passed; the player either fills a gap or redeals when blocked.',
      bid: 'No bidding mechanism exists in Gaps.',
      meld: 'Gaps is not a meld-making game; cards are sequenced directly on tableau rows.',
      go_out: 'Game ends on solved layout or no redeals left, not by a go-out action.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Finish with each row in same-suit order from 2 through King, leaving the four gaps immediately to the right of the Kings.',
      'Turn-flow example: A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
      'Scoring example: Gaps is normally scored as solved or unsolved; some software also reports cards correctly ordered. All four rows are complete suit sequences from 2 through King with final gaps to the right of each King..',
